0.75 0.8 0.78 RG 0.6 w 48 251.89 m 547.28 251.89 l S
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 48 229.89 Td (Schedule 2 asks for a full employment history with a satisfactory written explanation of any gap. You have found) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 48 215.39 Td (one. Here is the conversation. It takes two minutes and it is not an accusation.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 60 195.89 Td ("While I was checking the files I noticed a gap in your work history, between [month] and [month]. I need) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 60 181.39 Td (to record what that period was, in your words. What were you doing then?") Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 48 161.89 Td (Write what they say, in their words, date it, and put it in the file. If they are not sure of the dates, record that they) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 48 147.39 Td (are not sure and what they can remember. If their account does not fit the rest of the history, ask again and) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 48 132.89 Td (follow it up; that is what "satisfactory" means. Never write an explanation for them.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F2 10 Tf 48 113.39 Td (The record is their account and your judgment of it, not a sentence for the sake of a sentence.) Tj ET
