BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 48 735.89 Td (Schedule 2 requires two written references, one from the most recent employer. Verifying them by phone is good) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 48 721.39 Td (practice, not a rule, and it is what turns a letter into something you have checked. Ring the organisation's main) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 48 706.89 Td (number, not the mobile on the letter, and ask for the person who signed it.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 60 687.39 Td ("Hello, I'm [name], manager at a children's home. [Person] has applied to work with us and gave us a) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 60 672.89 Td (reference in your name. Can I take two minutes to confirm it? Did you write it? Can you confirm the dates) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 60 658.39 Td (they worked with you, and their role? Why did they leave? And the one I have to ask: would you employ) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10.5 Tf 60 643.89 Td (them again, in work around children?") Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 48 624.39 Td (Then two lines on paper: who you spoke to, when, and what they confirmed. Date it, initial it, staple it to the) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F1 10 Tf 48 609.89 Td (reference. That note is your record of the check.) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F2 10 Tf 48 590.39 Td (If the referee hesitates on the last question, that hesitation is the most useful thing the call could have) Tj ET
BT 0.1 0.12 0.11 rg /F2 10 Tf 48 575.89 Td (given you. Follow it.) Tj ET
